  "name": "Medicine Ball Rotational Slam",
  "definition": "A unilateral standing power repetition that winds a two-hand slam-safe medicine ball from one hip up and around overhead, then reverses through trunk rotation and flexion to release it into the floor outside the opposite foot. Both mirrored directions are prescribed. Straight overhead slams, wall throws, retained-ball chops, seated twists, and repetitions without a back-foot pivot remain outside this family.",
